      "wk-faq": {
        "type": "wk-faq",
        "settings": {
          "eyebrow": "Questions, answered",
          "heading": "The honest answers",
          "subhead": "No spin, no over-promising. If something isn't here, our team reads every message.",
          "q1": "I'm not sure I'm in perimenopause yet — is this for me?",
          "a1": "Most likely, yes. Perimenopause can begin in your early forties — often years before the word menopause feels like it belongs to you. If you're noticing changes in sleep, mood, bloating, or temperature and a doctor has told you your labs are \"normal,\" this formula was built for exactly that window.*",
          "q2": "I'm already in menopause — is it too late for this to help?",
          "a2": "No. The transition doesn't end at your last period — hot flashes, night sweats, and disrupted sleep often continue for years beyond it. The botanicals and gut-hormone support work on the same systems whichever side of that line you're on.*",
          "q3": "Does it contain hormones?",
          "a3": "No. There is no estrogen, progesterone, or any hormone in this formula. It works through named botanicals, vitamins, and a probiotic blend that support your body's own systems — including the gut bacteria that metabolise estrogen — rather than adding hormones to them.*",
          "q4": "Can I take it with HRT, birth control, or my medications?",
          "a4": "Every ingredient and dose is named on the label, so you and your clinician can review it in full. Some botanicals — black cohosh and chasteberry among them — can interact with certain medications and hormone therapies, so check with your provider before starting if you're on HRT or hormonal birth control, taking medication, pregnant, or nursing.",
          "q5": "Are there any side effects?",
          "a5": "It's hormone-free and sugar-free, with every active at a researched dose rather than a mega-dose, and it's generally well tolerated. Some women notice mild digestive shifts in the first week as the probiotic blend settles in — that usually passes. If anything persists, stop and check with your healthcare provider.",
          "q6": "How is this different from a multivitamin or other menopause supplements?",
          "a6": "Most of the category hides behind proprietary blends and fairy-dust doses. We name and dose every active at the level the research actually used — 200mg ashwagandha, 100mg standardised black cohosh, 100mg red clover isoflavones, and a 10 billion CFU probiotic blend. You can read exactly what you're taking, and how much, on the panel.",
          "q7": "When will I notice a difference?",
          "a7": "Many women report steadier sleep and a calmer stress response within two to three weeks. Bloating and mood often follow by week four, with the fuller picture — cooler nights, steadier days — by weeks six to eight as the actives reach steady state. Consistency matters more than timing.*",
          "q8": "How do I take it — and what does it taste like?",
          "a8": "Two gummies a day, with or without food, at whatever moment sticks — no loading phase. Each bottle is 60 gummies, a full 30-day supply. The gummy is a deep-red cranberry, lightly tart rather than candy-sweet — no added sugar, no sugar alcohols, vegan and non-GMO.",
          "q9": "How does the subscription work, and what if it's not for me?",
          "a9": "Your subscription ships free on your chosen cadence, and you can pause, skip, or cancel anytime from your account — no emails, no hoops. And because the formula needs a full transition cycle to show what it can do, every order is backed by our 90-day money-back guarantee: take the whole three months, and if it isn't right for you, reach out for a full refund — no need to return the bottles."
        }
      },
